                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Overall Recommended: ✅\nGameplay: ❤️🤍🤍\nGraphics: ❤️❤️❤️\nStory: ❤️❤️🤍\nMusic/Sounds: ❤️❤️🤍\nJumpscares: ❎\nBugs: ✅\n--------------------------------\nTotal: ❤️❤️❤️🤍\n\ncomment: As a warning, I'm a bit more harsh when it comes to VNs and dialogue issues. Marianne's name tends to be spelled \"Mary Anne\" with only Hannah (she's meant to get names wrong but Marianne and Mary Anne are pronounced the same, so having a visual difference is odd and pointless). Voice over doesn't always match the written text. There are some text/story errors (such as repetitous errors, \"she must have kept some of what I said in mind\" twice within 3 lines of text; or Isabella mentions Zach never meeting Rose after choosing to meet with a priest and they both encounter Rose). Some other little bits within the dialogue seem a bit odd but are not really noticeable nor change how the story comes across (such as the idea that fish and chips is unheard of in America as if it's not also a [somewhat] common dish over there too). Also the intro disclaimer mispells the word \"coincidental\". The biggest bug is the game will close during two different points within Ashton's route when using instant skip if certain choices are made during a playthrough (not sure which choices trigger the bug though). \n\nOverall, I enjoyed the story even though one character made me feel bad for them during the true ending when no one really should given that they are NOT a good person at all (sometimes redemption arcs can be a good thing but they felt a bit too far gone to be properly redeemed). Getting 100% in all the routes is extremely grindy and pretty tedious as most of the routes are the same thing just with slightly different choices or character combos. It would be amazing if the skip continued after each choice as well for the end game clean up.",
